cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "TDMM: Bayesian Time-Dynamic Mixed-Effects Models for Longitudinal Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Grigsby
    given-names: Makena
  - family-names: Kürüm
    given-names: Esra
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/esrakurum/Bayesian-TDMM"
abstract: "TDMM provides Bayesian time-dynamic regression models for Gaussian, Bernoulli, and Poisson outcomes. Coefficients vary smoothly over time, with an optional subject-specific random intercept for repeated observations. Models without a random intercept support independent observations."
keywords:
  - Bayesian modeling
  - longitudinal data
  - time-varying coefficients
  - mixed-effects models
  - P-splines
  - JAGS
